        "observation": "## ACC Football Archive – Column Headers & Filters\n\n### Nine Column Headers (Left to Right)\n1. **Team**\n2. **Date**\n3. **Opponent**\n4. **Number**\n5. **Player**\n6. **Initial Status**\n7. **Update 1 Status**\n8. **Update 2 Status**\n9. **Game Day Status**\n\n### Evidence of Visibility\nAll nine headers are rendered as visible HTML elements on the page. Each header is wrapped in a `` tag and appears as a clickable column-sort button. The headers are visible above the data rows without any scrolling required for the first six columns; the last three columns (Update 1 Status, Update 2 Status, Game Day Status) may require horizontal scrolling if the table overflows, but they are still rendered and labeled.\n\n### Date/Season Filters (Visible on Page)\n- **\"View Seasons Prior to 2026\"** – A button to access archive seasons before the current 2026 season.\n- **\"Filter by Week\"** – Text input field for filtering by week number.\n- **\"Filter by Team\"** – Text input field for filtering by team name.\n- **\"Filter by Player\"** – Text input field for filtering by player name.\n- **\"Go\"** – Submit button to apply the above filters.\n\n### Status Labels\nThe statuses shown in the table data (based on sample rows such as Boston College players vs. Virginia Tech on 9/26/26) include:\n- **Questionable**\n- **Available**\n- **Out**\n\nThese correspond to the three status columns: **Initial Status**, **Update 1 Status**, and **Update 2 Status**, followed by **Game Day Status**.\n\n**Note:** The task instruction requested that statuses only be reported \"if explicitly shown.\" The column headers themselves are labeled \"Initial Status,\" \"Update 1 Status,\" and \"Update 2 Status,\" which directly map to the meanings *Initial*, *Update 1*, and *Update 2*. \"Game Day Status\" is the fourth status column. The status values observed in the data (Questionable, Available, Out) are sample values and not a definitive exhaustive list of all possible status values across the entire archive.\n\n### Conclusion\nAll nine column headers are **visible and labeled**. No headers were omitted or required inference. The date/season filters are clearly present as described above.",
